  "details": "VRChat 2023.2.2 beta build 1301 changes the ordering of the \"Send Invite\" button on the user page of the Main Menu. So, now it is consistent in joinable and in-private cases each other. It's nice.\n\nHow about extending the consistency between QM and MM? Currently, the order is opposite (see attached images 1, 2).\n\nExtended idea: How about disabling the button instead of hiding it? If so, people can point the buttons more quickly without misoperation since the operations are constantly bound to the places. Also, the disabled button can have a tooltip text, and people can get information about why it is unavailable now (see attached image 3).\n\nAdditional report: The release note says `Ordering of \"Send Invite\" button on QM user page is now consistent with \"Request Invite\" and \"Join\"`. But the change is on MM, not QM.",
